## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical CBA for a local-first search feature, balancing storage, CPU, and privacy.

## Key Concepts
- On-device indexing
- Delta sync costs
- Privacy/compliance
- Update cadence and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
function indexRepo(files) {
  // naive tokenization
  const index = {};
  for (const f of files) {
    const tokens = f.content.split(/\\W+/).filter(Boolean);
    tokens.forEach(t => (index[t] ||= []).push(f.path));
  }
  return index;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure user time saved and energy impact to validate the break-even?
- How would you design for monorepos and very large repos with incremental indexing?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a privacy-preserving, on-device ML feature with a clear financial rationale and real-world constraints.

## Key Concepts

- On-device ML size/latency trade-offs
- Energy, memory, and storage budgeting for mobile apps
- Telemetry costs and delta-based model updates
- Regulatory/compliance costs and risk assessment
- Go/no-go criteria and break-even planning

## Code Example

```javascript
function inferLeadScore(features, model) {
  // simple LR-like dot product
  let score = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < features.length; i++) {
    score += features[i] * model.weights[i];
  }
  return 1 / (1 + Math.exp(-score));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate drift and schedule model updates offline?
- How would you audit privacy, regulatory compliance, and data minimization during rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses cost-aware design of privacy-preserving observability with edge processing, cross-region deployment, and go/no-go decisions.

## Key Concepts
- Edge compute budgeting
- Privacy-first telemetry
- Data retention and regional regulations
- Multi-region cost models
- Rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function cba(params) {
  // simple cost model
  const deviceCost = params.deviceCPU * 0.1 + params.deviceMem * 0.05;
  const deltaCost = (params.deltaKB / 1024) * 0.02;
  const centralCost = params.retentionMonths * 1000 * 0.01;
  return deviceCost + deltaCost + centralCost;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for GDPR/CCPA across regions?
- What metrics would tie cost to business value beyond raw savings?

## Why This Is Asked

Balances privacy, regulatory needs, and system load by moving KYC attestation on-device.

### Key Concepts

- On-device cryptography and attestation
- Data minimization and privacy
- Key management and rotation
- Compliance and auditability

### Code Example

```javascript
async function signAttestation(privateKey, payload) {
  const enc = new TextEncoder();
  const data = enc.encode(JSON.stringify(payload));
  const sig = await crypto.subtle.sign({name: 'ECDSA', hash: 'SHA-256'}, privateKey, data);
  return btoa(String.fromCharCode(...new Uint8Array(sig)));
}
```

### Follow-up Questions

- How to handle key compromise and revocation?
- What metrics drive break-even and rollout schedule?
- How to prevent replay attacks and ensure forward secrecy?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to build a holistic CBA for an in-car edge AI feature, balancing real-time compute, OTA updates, data privacy, and regulatory compliance, while accounting for drift, validation, and fault tolerance.

## Key Concepts

- Fleet-level TCO across devices and software layers
- Edge compute energy and thermal constraints
- OTA bandwidth, update cadence, rollback strategies
- Privacy, data minimization, regulatory logs
- Drift monitoring, validation pipelines, go/no-go criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple illustrative cost model for 18-month CBA
function tco18m({fleetSize, perVehicleStateGB, energyW, otaMinorMB, otaMajorMB, driftCost, validationCost, rollbackCost, upliftPerMonth}) {
  const hardwareCost = fleetSize * perVehicleStateGB; // placeholder units
  const monthlyEnergyCost = fleetSize * energyW * 24 * 30; // approximate energy cost in Wh per month
  const otaCost = fleetSize * (otaMinorMB * 0.001 + otaMajorMB * 0.01); // hypothetical cost units
  const drift = fleetSize * driftCost;
  const validation = fleetSize * validationCost;
  const rollback = fleetSize * rollbackCost;
  const total = hardwareCost + monthlyEnergyCost + otaCost + drift + validation + rollback;
  const breakEvenMonths = total / upliftPerMonth;
  return { total, breakEvenMonths };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the drift model and set driftCost thresholds? 
- What metrics tie CBA to safety/regulatory requirements and how would you incorporate them? 
- How would you handle market/regulatory changes affecting privacy costs?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model a device-resident telemetry system that serves multiple apps while enforcing data minimization and consent, balancing privacy, UX impact, and backend savings.

## Key Concepts

- Data deduplication and cross-app coordination on-device
- Consent lifecycle and policy enforcement across tenants
- On-device aggregation, sampling, and energy budgeting
- Privacy/compliance costs and drift monitoring
- Rollout strategy, break-even analysis, and governance

## Code Example

```javascript
function aggregateDeltas(deltas) {
  // de-duplicate by user/app+event, then sample
  const seen = new Set();
  const out = [];
  for (const d of deltas) {
    const key = d.userId + '|' + d.appId + '|' + d.eventId;
    if (!seen.has(key)) {
      seen.add(key);
      if (Math.random() < d.sampleRate) out.push(d.aggregate);
    }
  }
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you quantify cross-app dedup cost vs backend savings?
- What would a staged rollout look like to minimize risk and ensure compliance?
